## Key Takeaways

This notebook demonstrates how NumPy provides the numerical foundation for Machine Learning and Deep Learning.

The main concepts learned include:

- Data is represented using multidimensional arrays or tensors
- Array shapes determine how data is organized
- Indexing and slicing allow specific data to be selected
- Element-wise operations are used for numerical transformations and activation functions
- Broadcasting allows efficient operations between compatible array shapes
- Matrix multiplication is the core computation inside neural-network layers
- Aggregation functions are used for statistics and loss calculations
- Reshaping allows tensors to be converted into different formats
- Random initialization provides neural-network weights with suitable starting values
- Vectorization makes numerical computations significantly faster
- Neural networks combine these NumPy concepts into a complete computation pipeline

---

## Why NumPy Matters for Deep Learning

NumPy introduces many of the same concepts later used in frameworks such as PyTorch and TensorFlow.

Important concepts include:

- Tensors
- Shapes
- Broadcasting
- Matrix multiplication
- Activation functions
- Reshaping
- Statistics
- Weight initialization
- Vectorization

Understanding these concepts in NumPy makes it easier to understand how deep-learning frameworks work internally.

