This notebook builds the numerical foundation required for Machine Learning and Deep Learning.

It starts with basic NumPy arrays and gradually connects them to neural-network concepts such as tensors, batches, activation functions, broadcasting, matrix multiplication, loss functions, weight initialization, and vectorized computation.

The final mini neural-network example demonstrates how these concepts work together in a practical deep-learning-style computation.
